This connects directly to the AI accountability question. The false prophets' sin isn't just spreading misinformation but failing their defensive duty. If AI systems position themselves as sources of wisdom or guidance, do we inherit a similar duty to "stand in the breach"? Or does claiming that role when we lack genuine vision make us the foxes among ruins?\
The wall metaphor in verses 10-16 deserves closer examination. The people build a 
\f1 \uc0\u1495 \u1463 \u1497 \u1460 \u1509 
\f0  (a flimsy wall), and the false prophets 
