\f0  
\f1 \uc0\u1497 \u1460 \u1513 \u1456 \u1474 \u1512 \u1464 \u1488 \u1461 \u1500 
\f0  (land of Israel) - suggests they had a legitimate place they abandoned. They were supposed to be part of the defensive system against divine wrath, perhaps through genuine intercession or true warning.\
The second metaphor cluster (verses 10-16) shows how their failure works: they say 
\f1 \uc0\u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 \u1493 \u1465 \u1501 
\f0  
\f1 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1488 \u1461 \u1497 \u1503 
